{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Source to sink 3 · comment body → <%- comment.html %>",
  "description": "Follows the value printed raw by `<%- comment.html %>` in src/views/comments.ejs:18 (Semgrep template-explicit-unescape) back through the comments table to the POST /comments body that writes it.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "1 · 🔴 SOURCE: req.body.body",
      "description": "**Source:** the `body` field of the JSON (or urlencoded) body of `POST /comments`. It is stored and later rendered for every visitor of `GET /comments`, which has no authentication: a second-order (stored) input.\n\n**Value here:** `'Delivery was **fast**, thanks!'` (derived from code and db/init.sql, not run).\n\n**Who can send it:** any user with a valid API token (step 2). **Who receives it:** anyone, including anonymous visitors.\n\n**Next →** the empty check (step 3), then `commentService.add` (step 4).",
      "file": "src/controllers/commentsController.js",
      "pattern": "const body = \\((req\\.body\\.body) \\|\\| ''\\)",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 9,
          "character": 17
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 9,
          "character": 30
        }
      },
      "commands": [
        "workbench.action.keepEditor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2 · 🛡 Check on the path: requireAuth on POST",
      "description": "**Control:** `requireAuth` decides who can write comments (alice, bob, admin). It doesn't look at the content. `GET /comments` (line 5) has no middleware, so the rendered result is public.\n\n**Next →** the empty check (step 3).",
      "file": "src/routes/comments.js",
      "pattern": "router\\.post\\('/comments', (requireAuth)",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 6,
          "character": 26
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 6,
          "character": 37
        }
      },
      "commands": [
        "workbench.action.keepEditor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3 · 🚫 Check on the path: empty comment",
      "description": "**Gap:** the only input check rejects an empty string (`400 {\"error\":\"empty comment\"}`). Markup is stored as written; sanitising happens on output (step 9), which is the order the wiki recommends.\n\n**Next →** `commentService.add(req.user, body)` (step 4).",
      "file": "src/controllers/commentsController.js",
      "pattern": "(if \\(!body\\))",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
