      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "8 · Markdown → HTML (marked)",
      "description": "**Propagates:** `marked` (16.4.2) turns Markdown into HTML. It does not escape or remove raw HTML in the input, so any markup the author typed is still present after this step.\n\n**Value here:** `'<p>Delivery was <strong>fast</strong>, thanks! …</p>'` (observed locally, see the report).\n\n**Next →** sanitised by DOMPurify (step 9).",
      "file": "src/utils/markdown.js",
      "pattern": "marked\\.parse\\((text)\\)",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 4,
          "character": 60
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 4,
          "character": 64
        }
